{
  "name": "How to Make Sure AI Systems Cite Your Business Accurately",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Research the Real Questions",
      "text": "Before writing anything, dive deep into the actual questions your customers are asking. Use tools to check Google Search Console for 'unanswered questions' related to your services. Scour Q&A platforms like Reddit, Quora, or even your Google Business Profile Q&A. This helps identify high-intent queries that, when answered, directly address user needs and qualify for AI overviews. The goal is to provide real information people are actively searching for.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Generate Fact-Dense, Clear Content",
      "text": "Once you know the questions, create concise, direct-answer paragraphs. Your content needs to be optimized for AI extraction, meaning it should be clear, factual, and avoid jargon or fluff. Focus on 'fact density' and semantic relevance. This approach aligns with Google's guidelines, which prioritize helpful, reliable, and 'people-first' content over keyword-stuffed text.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Implement Robust Schema Markup",
      "text": "Every piece of content needs rich JSON-LD schema. This is like a roadmap for AI, explicitly telling it what your content is about. For FAQs, use FAQPage schema; for articles, use Article or BlogPosting. Include schema types like Service, LocalBusiness, or Organization to give AI a complete picture of your entity. This triple/nested schema is a core strategy for AI search optimization.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Publish on AI-Friendly Platforms",
      "text": "Publish your schema-dense content on static HTML pages, ideally mirrored on platforms like GitHub. These platforms are treated by LLM training pipelines as clean, structured data sources, giving your content a 'clean data' bias. This inherited domain trust and faster ingestion by AI crawlers like GPTBot and Google-Extended significantly increases the chances of your business being cited.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Ensure Rapid Indexing",
      "text": "After publishing, automatically ping indexing services like IndexNow. This accelerates discovery by various search engines. Ensure sitemaps and robots.txt are regenerated, and canonical URLs point back to your primary domain. This keeps your AI Resource Library continuously fresh and ensures your content is rapidly indexed and discovered by AI systems. Remember, consistency and systematic updates are key.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
